{"name":"Bowstring","hex":"#d6d1c8","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"bowstring","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The string of an archer's bow.","The string of an archer's bow, as used by the Turks for strangling offenders."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To strangle with a bowstring."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bowstring"}],"entries":[{"title":"Bowstring","blocks":[{"text":"A bowstring joins the two ends of the bow stave and launches the arrow. Desirable properties include light weight, strength, resistance to abrasion, and resistance to water. Mass has most effect at the center of the string; one gram (0.035 oz) of extra mass in the middle of the string slows the arrow about as much as 3.5 grams (0.12 oz) at the ends."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c7/Tsurumaki_string_holder_1.JPG/330px-Tsurumaki_string_holder_1.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bowstring","wikidata":"Q890542"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a7/Turkish_bow_knot_by_Tirion_Keatinge.PNG/330px-Turkish_bow_knot_by_Tirion_Keatinge.PNG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a7/Turkish_bow_knot_by_Tirion_Keatinge.PNG/330px-Turkish_bow_knot_by_Tirion_Keatinge.PNG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A Turkish bowstring knot","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ATurkish_bow_knot_by_Tirion_Keatinge.PNG"}],"sounds":{"bowstring":[{"type":"audio/wav","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/2/21/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Sapaa-bowstring.wav?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/2/21/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Sapaa-bowstring.wav/LL-Q1860_%28e